{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Check your inbox{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <h1>Check your inbox</h1>

    {# DELIBERATELY STATIC, AND DELIBERATELY ADDRESS-FREE.

       This page is the destination for two very different journeys — a successful registration and
       *every* submission of the resend form — and it must look identical from both. "We sent a link
       to name@example.com" would be friendlier and would break the design: the address would have to
       arrive here somehow (session, flash, query string), and a page that varies at all between the
       four AC-15 cases reintroduces the enumeration oracle the resend controller exists to close, at
       the very last step. There is nothing dynamic in this file, so there is nothing to leak.

       Unstyled, like the rest of slice 1 and 2. ADR-0006's SCSS system arrives with the first real
       layout; marking this up by hand now would only be thrown away then. #}
    <p>If an account needs verifying at the address you gave us, a message with a confirmation link
        is on its way. Open the link to finish setting your account up, then sign in.</p>

    <p>The link works once and expires after 24 hours.</p>

    <p>Nothing arrived? It can take a minute, and it is worth checking your spam folder — then
        <a href="{{ path('app_verify_email_resend') }}">ask us to send another one</a>.</p>

    <p><a href="{{ path('app_login') }}">Back to sign in</a></p>
{% endblock %}
